<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Octo performance lab — {{ vars.name }}</title>
<style>
  :root { color-scheme: light dark; }
  body { font: 16px/1.55 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", system-ui, sans-serif;
         margin: 0; padding: 2.5rem 1.25rem; background: #fbfbfd; color: #16181d; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { background: #0e1014; color: #e7e9ee; } }
  main { max-width: 46rem; margin: 0 auto; }
  h1 { font-size: 1.9rem; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 0 0 0.35rem; }
  .sub { opacity: 0.68; margin: 0 0 2rem; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 1.25rem 0; font-size: 0.94rem; }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: 0.5rem 0.7rem; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(128,128,128,0.22); }
  th { font-weight: 600; opacity: 0.72; width: 42%; }
  code { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.88em; }
  .card { border: 1px solid rgba(128,128,128,0.22); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.1rem 1.35rem; margin: 1.1rem 0; }
  footer { margin-top: 2.5rem; font-size: 0.85rem; opacity: 0.6; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
  <h1>Hello, {{ vars.name }}</h1>
  <p class="sub">Rendered by an Octo <code>template-resource</code> block and served as raw
  <code>text/html</code> — no JSON anywhere in the response.</p>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>Request</h2>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Path parameter <code>name</code></th><td>{{ vars.name }}</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Name length</th><td>{{ size(vars.name) }} characters</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Looks like a hostname</th><td>{{ vars.name.matches("^[a-z0-9-]+$") }}</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Starts with &ldquo;oc&rdquo;</th><td>{{ vars.name.startsWith("oc") }}</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Event id</th><td><code>{{ eventID }}</code></td></tr>
      <tr><th>Rendered at</th><td>{{ now }}</td></tr>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>What this page measures</h2>
    <p>This is scenario <code>001-template-page</code> of the Octo performance lab. Each request
    exercises the full inbound path: the HTTP server connector accepts the connection, the HTTP
    route source matches <code>/page/&#123;name&#125;</code> and lifts the path parameter into the
    message variables, a flow worker picks the message off the channel, and the
    <code>template-resource</code> block evaluates every CEL placeholder in this document before
    the response is written back as raw content.</p>
    <p>Because there is no database, no outbound call, and no logging in the hot path, the number
    that comes out is close to the runtime's floor for an HTTP-in, HTML-out integration. That
    makes it a good regression canary: if this gets slower between Octo versions, something in the
    core request path got slower.</p>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Service</th><td>perf-template-page</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Connector</th><td><code>http</code> (HTTP Server)</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Source</th><td><code>http</code> route <code>/page/&#123;name&#125;</code></td></tr>
      <tr><th>Block</th><td><code>template-resource</code>, raw body, <code>text/html</code></td></tr>
      <tr><th>Greeting echo</th><td>{{ "hello " + vars.name + ", you are visitor number " + string(size(vars.name) * 7) }}</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Correlation id</th><td><code>{{ correlationID }}</code></td></tr>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>Tuning knobs under comparison</h2>
    <p>The baseline arm of this benchmark declares none of these and takes Octo's defaults. The
    tuned arm sets them explicitly, and <code>task sweep</code> grid-searches them.</p>
    <table>
      <tr><th><code>workers</code></th><td>Consumers pulling from this flow's message channel. Default 8.</td></tr>
      <tr><th><code>buffer</code></th><td>Channel depth before publishers block. Default 64.</td></tr>
      <tr><th><code>pool</code></th><td>Shared worker pool for concurrent composites. Default 8.</td></tr>
    </table>
  </div>

  <footer>
    octo-performance · scenario 001 · generated {{ now }} for {{ vars.name }}
  </footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
